WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
Good morning, John. I woke up this morning at nine o'clock.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:05.819
This is me looking at myself in the Viewscreen and thinking, "My hair is a bird,"

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:08.669
"your argument is invalid." Then I went for a run.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.960
And I looked at some fish and then because it was so frackin hot and humid, I jumped into a pool. I'm in Florida.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.969
It's very hot everywhere. The air isn't "conditioned". Blow your frigid air of sweet salvation.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:23.850
And because the inside is so preferable to the outside, no one is outside. Everyone is stuck in their

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:30.000
4,000 cubic foot SUVs, and that includes me. The people at Enterprise rental car excitedly announced that I was getting a

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.939
"quadruple upgrade" to a "real big truck". It is indeed real big, though in Montana,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.759
we don't call something a truck unless you can throw a bull elk in the back of it.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.710
I'd call this thing a boat before I call it a truck.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.629
I lived here most of my life, and then having moved away,

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:45.040
I realized that there were a lot of things wrong with it.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:50.020
Now, I'm realizing that I kind of had a rather selective negative memory about this place

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.180
Yes, it is unnecessarily hot. Yes,

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:53.260
the sun is

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.070
ridiculously bright.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:59.279
Can somebody turn this down? The cars are big and you need to have one all the time to get anywhere. All the cups are made

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.820
of styrofoam and the fire ants...yeah, the fire ants are bad. You should not go poke fire ant mounds because

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:11.220
Well, wow yeah, okay? Yeah? I got stung, but I can't really say I didn't deserve that one, but there are also things

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.600
I love. Sweet tea, Waffle House, and that giant insane sun breeds a

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:22.580
humongous variety of life that we just can't compare with in Montana. And sure the humidity will suck away your will to live, but sometimes

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.380
it's nice to have a reason to jump into a giant pool of water.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.360
But now that the sun is going down and the temperature is approaching

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:34.940
bearable, at least, I realize that the reason I feel like I miss Florida now isn't because I miss Florida,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.240
it's because I missed the reason that I'm here right now.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.849
And I'm here to watch a friend get married, and so of course all of my old college friends from Florida are also here to

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:42.869
watch my friend get married.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:46.438
It's a reunion of sorts, several people who I haven't seen in almost 10 years.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.200
Which is how long it has been since I graduated from college which is extraordinarily

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.740
upsetting. Most of the best reasons to love a place are people. And when I walked out of the Tallahassee regional airport and the thick,

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.030
hot air was blowing

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:04.828
through the palm trees, the thing I think about first isn't the traffic, or the sprawl.

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:09.449
It's actually the reason why I had to walk away from the pool, because I didn't want my friends to hear me get all sappy

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.319
about this stuff.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:13.619
But the reason I love Florida is because of the people

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:19.529
who I loved when I was here, and who I will of course keep on loving forever. John, I'll see you on Wednesday.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.220
The fries are tiny too. The fries are tiny, cuz they're Steak and Shake fries.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.780
Off camera: The fries have not changed at all.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.760
Okay

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.140
Off camera: Oh, oh, he did it, wow. That was two bites.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.860
Off camera: There was look compression

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.040
Off camera: Don't die.

